✗ Individual findings (6)
────────────────────

 LOW   ISSUE-307  Checkout persists credentials in .git/config (latent)
       │
       └──▶ job `publish` from workflow `release.yml`: runs "actions/checkout@v4" without
            `persist-credentials: false`
            ↳ at https://github.com/getplumber-examples/plumber-cli-e2e/blob/findings/.github/workflows/release.yml#L15

       So     GITHUB_TOKEN lingers in .git/config (latent; becomes a leak if a later step packs .git
              into an artifact or runs fork-controlled code)
       Fix    set persist-credentials: false on the checkout
       ↳ docs: https://getplumber.io/docs/cli/issues/ISSUE-307

  ┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄

 HIGH  ISSUE-702  Action is hosted in an archived repository
       │
       └──▶ job `release-notes` from workflow `build.yml`: references "actions/create-release@v1"
            whose upstream repository is archived
            ↳ at https://github.com/getplumber-examples/plumber-cli-e2e/blob/findings/.github/workflows/build.yml#L27

       So     no security patches are coming
       Fix    replace the archived action
       ↳ docs: https://getplumber.io/docs/cli/issues/ISSUE-702

  ┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄

 HIGH  ISSUE-803  Excessive workflow permissions (2 findings)
       │
       ├──▶ job `auto-approve` from workflow `ci.yml`: runs with overly broad permissions:
       │    "write-all"
       │    ↳ at https://github.com/getplumber-examples/plumber-cli-e2e/blob/findings/.github/workflows/ci.yml#L9
       └──▶ job `publish` from workflow `release.yml`: runs with overly broad permissions:
            "write-all"
            ↳ at https://github.com/getplumber-examples/plumber-cli-e2e/blob/findings/.github/workflows/release.yml#L8

       Fix    narrow the permissions to what the job needs
       ↳ docs: https://getplumber.io/docs/cli/issues/ISSUE-803

  ┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄

 CRIT  ISSUE-203  Pipeline enables CI debug trace
       │
       └──▶ job `auto-approve` from workflow `ci.yml`: sets the debug variable `ACTIONS_STEP_DEBUG`
            to "true".
            ↳ at https://github.com/getplumber-examples/plumber-cli-e2e/blob/findings/.github/workflows/ci.yml#L13

       Fix    turn off the CI debug trace
       ↳ docs: https://getplumber.io/docs/cli/issues/ISSUE-203

  ┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄

 CRIT  ISSUE-410  Security job weakened
       │
       └──▶ Security job `build/security-scan` is weakened by `allow_failure: true`, which masks
            scan failures.
            ↳ at https://github.com/getplumber-examples/plumber-cli-e2e/blob/findings/.github/workflows/build.yml#L35

       Fix    restore the security job's settings
       ↳ docs: https://getplumber.io/docs/cli/issues/ISSUE-410

────────────────────
✗ Attack paths (7)
────────────────────

 LOW   Attack path 7
       Entry  github.event.pull_request.title (user-controlled input injected in a script)
       │
       └──▶ runs in job `build` from workflow `ci.yml`
            └─▶ reaches code execution on the runner, no secret and no write token

       So     as anyone who can open a pull request, an attacker can execute code on the runner
              and poison what it caches or uploads
       Fix    pass the input through an environment variable
       ↳ details: run `plumber explain -a 7`

  ┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄

 LOW   Attack path 6
       Entry  github.event.workflow_run.head_sha (code of another workflow's run checked out)
       │
       └──▶ runs in job `comment` from workflow `dangerous.yml` (on workflow_run)
            └─▶ reaches code execution on the runner; nothing else proven

       So     as anyone who opens a pull request,
              an attacker can execute code on an ephemeral runner
       Fix    never check out the pull request head in a privileged workflow
       ↳ details: run `plumber explain -a 6`

  ┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄

 MED   Attack path 5
       Entry  node:latest (mutable image tag, source not checked on GitHub)
       │
       └──▶ runs in job `build` from workflow `ci.yml`
            └─▶ reaches every secret of the repository,
                        a token with push, publish and deploy access and write access to actions,
                        pull requests and security events and an OIDC token

       So     if this image is compromised or malicious,
              an attacker can read every secret of the repository, push in your repository,
              publish packages and deploy
       Fix    pin the image by digest
       ↳ details: run `plumber explain -a 5`

  ┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄

 HIGH  Attack path 4
       Entry  https://get.example.com/install.sh (script downloaded and run at build time)
       │
       └──▶ runs in job `build` from workflow `ci.yml`
            └─▶ reaches every secret of the repository,
                        a token with push, publish and deploy access and write access to actions,
                        pull requests and security events and an OIDC token

       So     if this script is compromised or malicious,
              an attacker can read every secret of the repository, push in your repository,
              publish packages and deploy
       Fix    download the script, check its checksum, then run it
       ↳ details: run `plumber explain -a 4`

  ┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄

 HIGH  Attack path 3 (unverified)
       Entry  dorny/paths-filter@1c9b1f1aaa22 (external action pinned to a commit that is not in its
              repository)
       │
       └──▶ runs in job `build` from workflow `ci.yml` (unverified)
            └─▶ reaches every secret of the repository,
                        a token with push, publish and deploy access and write access to actions,
                        pull requests and security events and an OIDC token

       So     through the commit this action is pinned to, which is not in its repository,
              an attacker can read every secret, push in your repository, publish packages
              and deploy
       Note   Plumber could not check what it runs
       Fix    pin a commit that exists in the action's repository
       ↳ details: run `plumber explain -a 3`

  ┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄

 CRIT  Attack path 2
       Entry  github.event.pull_request.head.sha (pull request code checked out in a privileged
              workflow)
       │
       └──▶ runs in job `preview` from workflow `pr-preview.yml` (on pull_request_target)
            └─▶ reaches a token with write access to pull requests

       So     as anyone who opens a pull request,
              an attacker can execute code to write to pull requests
       Fix    never check out the pull request head in a privileged workflow
       ↳ details: run `plumber explain -a 2`

  ┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄┄

 CRIT  Attack path 1
       Entry  tj-actions/changed-files@v45.0.0 (external action with a known vulnerability)
       │
       └──▶ runs in job `build` from workflow `ci.yml`
            └─▶ reaches every secret of the repository,
                        a token with push, publish and deploy access and write access to actions,
                        pull requests and security events and an OIDC token

       So     through the known vulnerability of this action,
              an attacker can read every secret of the repository, push in your repository,
              publish packages and deploy
       Fix    move to a version without the advisory
       ↳ details: run `plumber explain -a 1`

